    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The only runnable test class is `AcceptanceTest` (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of existing owners sharing the same first and last name (case-insensitively) at the moment an owner is created \u2014 following the same patterns the codebase already uses for `customerCode` and `householdId`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` (int32, min 0) property to the `Owner` schema. This drives regeneration of `OwnerDto`, which MapStruct maps automatically since the name matches the model field.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `namesake_count` column field with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 in `saveOwner`, for a new owner whose count isn't yet set, capture the count via a small private `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)` helper (with a `equalsIgnoreCase` null-safe helper). Because the owner isn't persisted yet, `findAll()` naturally reflects the \"before this create\" state. This mirrors the adjacent `customerCode` assignment rather than sprawling into new responsibilities.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column so the field persists across all supported databases (tests use hsqldb).\n\nThe value is a snapshot frozen at creation (persisted, not recomputed on read), which is what \"before this create\" requires \u2014 so in the test, owner *b* correctly reports `namesakeCount = 1` (owner *a*) while *a* stays at 0.",
